<title>SINGAPORE: Bangladesh sells fuel oil to BP at minus $12.45/T.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh sells fuel oil to BP at minus $12.45/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Bangladesh Petroleum Corp (BPC) has awarded its tender to sell 20,000 tonnes of fuel oil to British Petroleum at a discount of $12.45 per tonne over Singapore spot quotes, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 3.5-percent sulphur fuel oil would be for August 10-12 loading on a free-on-board Chittagong basis, they said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 8703571)</p>
</text>
